"notes": "Village of Cairo; governmental activities modified cash basis, business-type (sewer, water, landfill) accrual; basis recorded as cash. Governmental funds: p5 Total Governmental Funds column. Beginning cash = total governmental fund balance Sept 30, 2024 (1,174,478, p5); ending_cash = total fund balance 1,519,921 (p5) so the roll-forward ties; actual cash and county treasurer cash on p4 is 1,522,919, the difference being payroll withholding liability 2,998. Governmental transfers: statement prints net 'Transfers from (to) other funds' 11,327 (General -3,350, Street +21,303, Debt Service -6,626), recorded as transfers_in 11,327 net. Business-type: p7 totals column; receipts = operating revenues 534,630 + interest 1,296 + gain on disposal 54,938 = 590,864 and disbursements = operating expenses 383,875 + nonoperating expenses (2,920 + 12,928 + 5,171) = 404,894 (no single printed total; computed); transfers_net -11,327; roll-forward 1,459,584 + 590,864 - 404,894 - 11,327 = 1,634,227. Cash flow statement (pp8-9) is proprietary and cash basis entity so proprietary left null. Balance sheet from Statement of Net Position (p1) Primary Government Total column; component unit (CRA) excluded. General Fund detail uses the Combining Statement of General Fund Departments (pp13-14, by department, nonzero lines only), which is more detailed than the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (p10, not recorded to avoid double counting; its actuals agree: revenues 719,559, expenditures 528,759, transfer to other fund -3,350). Street and Sales Tax funds recorded from their budgetary comparison schedules (pp11-12, with final budget). Department interfund transfers net to -3,350 (1,781 General, -5,131 Community Center). No schedule for Debt Service Fund. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
